<?xml version="1.0"?>
<body language="English">
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00000" index="0">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The train hasn’t come in...\rI know! I’ll carry the passengers on\nmy back!\rThat won’t work.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00001" index="1">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The Magnet Train is back in service!\rPassengers need to go through the\ngate for the automatic ticket check...\r</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00002" index="2">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">...Beep!\rI am so sorry, but you need a\nMagnet Train Pass to get on\fthe Magnet Train...\r</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00003" index="3">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Passengers need to go through the\ngate for the automatic ticket check...\r</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00004" index="4">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ping...fwip!\nHere is your Pass back.\rThis train is about to leave\nfor Saffron City.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00005" index="5">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Enjoy the attractive and magnetic\njourney!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00006" index="6">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">We are arriving at Goldenrod!\nGoldenrod! The accent is on the “o”!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00007" index="7">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Enjoy the attractive and magnetic\njourney!\r</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00008" index="8">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">I’m the President.\rMy dream was to build a train that\nis faster than any Pokémon.\rIt really brings Johto much closer\nto Kanto.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00009" index="9">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">We request that you make sure you\nrefrain from keeping large Pokémon out\fat the station.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00010" index="10">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Magnet Train to Saffron, departing\nshortly. Passes, please.\r...None? The pass office is--well.\nIt’s in Saffron.\rI know exactly how that sounds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00011" index="11">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Magnet Train to Saffron, departing\nshortly. Passes, please.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00012" index="12">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">MEL: Two. Press. They’re with\nme--witness on the Azalea story,\ffully cleared, we’re on a\ndeadline.\rDon’t say anything. You don’t\nhave a pass, I have a pass, the\fdifference is a sentence I’m\nvery good at saying.\rKeep walking. Window seat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00013" index="13">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">...Press. Sure.\nEverybody’s press this week.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00014" index="14">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">MEL: Okay. Window’s yours. People\nalways think they won’t want the\fwindow and then they spend the\nwhole ride looking out it.\rLook--there, see how the country\nchanges? You can almost see where\fJohto stops being Johto.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00015" index="15">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">MEL: So here’s what I’ve\nactually got, and it’s not much.\rSilph’s research partnerships\nhave been expanding. Quietly. Into\fplaces research doesn’t usually\ngo.\rThe Ruins of Alph. Your well. A\ncouple of sites up north I’ve\fonly got rumors on.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00016" index="16">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">MEL: I don’t have a theory. I\nwant to be SO clear about that.\rI have THREADS. Just threads.\nThings that shouldn’t be near\feach other that keep turning up\nholding hands.\rAnd I cannot leave a thread alone.\nIt’s a medical condition. Ask\fanyone who’s ever worked with me.\nAsk anyone who’s ever DATED me.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00017" index="17">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">MEL: But that coat. The Silph\ncoat. That’s not a thread,\fthat’s a KNOT.\rAnd it came out of a kid’s\nmemory, off a forest road, which\fmeans it’s clean--nobody coached\nyou, you just SAW it.\rA person who just saw the thing\nand says the thing. Don’t ever\flose that. The job ruins it\neventually.\fHang onto it as long as you can.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0587_T25R0501_00018" index="18">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Magnet Train to Saffron.\nPasses, please.\r...The fare office is in Saffron.\nYes. I know how that sounds.</language>
	</row>
</body>
